# GitHub commit identity (TrendPlan)

For all git commits in this repo (and when pushing to GitHub for Vercel):

- **Author email:** `mr.habiibullahm@gmail.com`
- **Author name:** `habibullahm`

Do **not** use the work email `muhammad.habiibullah@dansmultipro.com` for commits. Vercel blocks deploys when GitHub cannot verify that account for the team.

When creating commits, set author via env for that commit if local config still has the work email:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="habibullahm" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="mr.habiibullahm@gmail.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="habibullahm" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="mr.habiibullahm@gmail.com" \
git commit ...
```

Prefer setting **local** (repo-only) `user.email` / `user.name` to the values above — never change global git config unless the user explicitly asks.
